ADVISORY BOARD AGREEMENT TEMPLATE
BCCS ECOSYSTEM - AVIATION COMPLIANCE PLATFORMS

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

ADVISORY BOARD MEMBER AGREEMENT

This Advisory Board Agreement ("Agreement") is entered into on [DATE] between [COMPANY NAME], a [STATE] corporation ("Company"), and [ADVISOR NAME] ("Advisor").

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. ADVISORY SERVICES

1.1 Scope of Services
Advisor agrees to provide strategic guidance and advice to Company in the following areas:
□ Aviation industry expertise and market insights
□ Regulatory compliance strategy and implementation
□ Business development and customer acquisition
□ Technology development and product strategy
□ Financial planning and fundraising guidance
□ Other: ________________________________

1.2 Time Commitment
Advisor commits to approximately [2-4] hours per month, including:
• Monthly advisory calls (1 hour)
• Email consultation and strategic input
• Introductions to potential customers, partners, or team members
• Review of key business documents and strategies

1.3 Term
This Agreement shall commence on [START DATE] and continue for [12-24] months, 
automatically renewable for additional [12] month periods unless terminated by 
either party with [30] days written notice.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

2. COMPENSATION STRUCTURE

Select One Compensation Model:

□ OPTION A: CASH RETAINER
Monthly retainer: $[1,000-2,500] per month
Annual total: $[12,000-30,000]
Payment terms: Net 30 days from invoice

□ OPTION B: REVENUE SHARE (PERFORMANCE-BASED)
Revenue percentage: [0.25-0.5]% of Company's gross revenue
Calculation period: Quarterly
Payment terms: Within 30 days of quarter end
Minimum threshold: Revenue share only applies when monthly revenue exceeds $[50,000]
Maximum cap: Annual payments not to exceed $[100,000-250,000]

□ OPTION C: SUCCESS-BASED FEES
Milestone-based compensation tied to specific achievements:
• Customer acquisition: $[2,500-5,000] per enterprise customer signed
• Fundraising success: [0.5-1.0]% of funds raised (if applicable)
• Strategic partnerships: $[10,000-25,000] per major partnership closed
• Product milestones: $[5,000-15,000] per major feature launch

□ OPTION D: DEFERRED COMPENSATION
Annual compensation: $[25,000-50,000]
Payment deferral: Until Company reaches sustained profitability
Interest rate: [6-8]% annually on deferred amounts
Maximum deferral period: [36] months

2.1 Expense Reimbursement
Company will reimburse Advisor for reasonable, pre-approved expenses directly 
related to advisory services, including travel for board meetings or customer 
introductions (with prior written approval).

2.2 No Equity Compensation
The parties acknowledge that Company's business model prioritizes founder equity 
retention through Revenue-Based Financing. Advisor agrees that no equity 
compensation will be provided under this Agreement.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

3. CONFIDENTIALITY AND NON-DISCLOSURE

3.1 Confidential Information
Advisor acknowledges access to Company's confidential information including:
• Financial data, projections, and business plans
• Technology specifications and intellectual property
• Customer lists, contracts, and pricing information
• Strategic plans and competitive intelligence
• Patent applications and regulatory strategies

3.2 Non-Disclosure Obligations
Advisor agrees to:
• Maintain strict confidentiality of all Company information
• Not disclose confidential information to third parties
• Use confidential information solely for advisory purposes
• Return all confidential materials upon Agreement termination

3.3 Survival
Confidentiality obligations survive termination of this Agreement for [5] years.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

4. CONFLICT OF INTEREST AND NON-COMPETE

4.1 Disclosure of Conflicts
Advisor warrants no existing conflicts of interest and agrees to immediately 
disclose any potential conflicts that may arise during the advisory relationship.

4.2 Non-Compete (Limited Scope)
During the term of this Agreement, Advisor agrees not to:
• Provide advisory services to direct competitors in aviation compliance software
• Invest in or join companies developing competing AI-powered regulatory platforms
• Solicit Company employees or customers for competing ventures

Exceptions: This restriction does not apply to:
• Passive investments in public companies or diversified funds
• Advisory roles in non-competing aviation sectors
• Consulting for regulatory agencies or educational institutions

4.3 Duration
Non-compete obligations expire [6-12] months after Agreement termination.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

5. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

5.1 Company Ownership
All intellectual property developed during advisory relationship belongs to Company, 
including:
• Improvements to existing Company IP
• New ideas or concepts developed collaboratively
• Strategic frameworks or methodologies created for Company

5.2 Advisor's Existing IP
Advisor retains ownership of pre-existing intellectual property and general 
industry knowledge not specific to Company's business.

5.3 Attribution
Company agrees to provide appropriate professional credit to Advisor for 
significant strategic contributions, where appropriate and non-confidential.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

6. PERFORMANCE EXPECTATIONS

6.1 Key Deliverables
Advisor's performance will be evaluated based on:
• Quality and relevance of strategic advice provided
• Responsiveness to Company requests and communications
• Success in making valuable introductions or connections
• Contribution to achieving specific milestones (if applicable)

6.2 Performance Review
Company will conduct quarterly performance reviews to assess:
• Advisory value delivered
• Goal achievement and milestone progress
• Continued alignment with Company objectives

6.3 Termination for Cause
Either party may terminate this Agreement immediately for:
• Material breach of confidentiality obligations
• Failure to perform advisory duties for [60] consecutive days
• Violation of non-compete provisions
• Conflicts of interest not properly disclosed

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

7. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

7.1 Advisory Capacity
Advisor serves in advisory capacity only and has no decision-making authority 
over Company operations, finances, or strategic direction.

7.2 Liability Limitation
Advisor's liability under this Agreement is limited to the total compensation 
received during the [12] months preceding any claim.

7.3 No Warranty
Advisor provides advice based on experience and judgment but makes no warranties 
regarding outcomes or results from following such advice.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

8. TERMINATION

8.1 Termination Rights
Either party may terminate this Agreement:
• With [30] days written notice for any reason
• Immediately for material breach after [10] days cure period
• Immediately for cause as defined in Section 6.3

8.2 Effect of Termination
Upon termination:
• All compensation payments cease (except accrued amounts)
• Confidentiality obligations remain in effect
• All Company property must be returned immediately
• Non-compete restrictions continue per Section 4.3

8.3 Survival
The following sections survive termination:
• Confidentiality (Section 3)
• Intellectual Property (Section 5)
• Limitation of Liability (Section 7)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

9. GENERAL PROVISIONS

9.1 Independent Contractor
Advisor is an independent contractor, not an employee, partner, or agent of Company.

9.2 Governing Law
This Agreement is governed by the laws of [STATE] without regard to conflict 
of law principles.

9.3 Dispute Resolution
Any disputes will be resolved through:
□ Binding arbitration under [STATE] arbitration rules
□ Mediation followed by litigation in [STATE] courts

9.4 Amendment
This Agreement may only be modified in writing signed by both parties.

9.5 Severability
If any provision is deemed invalid, the remainder of the Agreement remains in effect.

9.6 Entire Agreement
This Agreement constitutes the entire understanding between the parties and 
supersedes all prior agreements or understandings.

